Forked on 19 November 2026 by Affluent Labs LLC for ZestSSH (4.0, RDP sound), and used in place of
the crates.io package through [patch.crates-io] in zest_native's Cargo.toml. What came from the
crate stays under its licence; our change follows this folder's licence too (MIT or Apache-2.0).

What changed against 0.11.0, and nothing else:

  - src/client.rs, src/pdu/mod.rs: the client's Training Confirm echoes the Training PDU's
    wPackSize, the size of the whole PDU ([MS-RDPEA] 2.2.3.2), where it sent the length of the
    data after the fields, 8 bytes short (TrainingPdu::pack_size, used by the PDU's encoder and
    the confirm). GNOME Remote Desktop rejects any other value and then plays no sound. Upstream
    IronRDP's own fix, f86e3c49f3 (#2294), line for line.
  - The package's Cargo.toml.orig, Cargo.lock and .cargo_vcs_info.json are left out: they are
    not used by a build from a path.
  - Long dashes in src/client.rs, src/pdu/mod.rs, src/server.rs are plain hyphens: this repository keeps
    none. No code changed by it.

When IronRDP releases the fix, this folder goes and the crate comes from crates.io again.
